Kill {creature:Sight of Surrender|Sights of Surrender}. You find them:
- in {wiki:Guzzlemaw Valley}, if the server did enough tasks in the previous days;
- on the {wiki:Silencer Plateau}, at the end of the raid of the Luring Silencers mission;
- in the {wiki:Dark Grounds}, north of the Upper Roshamuul depot, which only open when the server completes 20 Soothing Bad Dreams tasks.

Look around the ruined city for the {item:Half-Buried Face|Half-Buried Faces}, giant faces sticking out of the ground. Only one part of the face has the right name (the **mouth**): use the {item:Broken Dream} on that part. Results:
- *"The Broken Dream crumbles in your hands."* — failed, you can try again straight away;
- *"Uh-oh. You mended a nightmare."* — failed and a {creature:Nightmare} spawns;
- *"A dream butterfly emerges and flits, flits, flits away. Hurray!"* — success, a {creature:Shimmying Butterfly} spawns.
After a Nightmare or a Shimmying Butterfly spawns, you have to wait 3 minutes before using that face again.

Go to the far **north-east** of Upper Roshamuul. On the mountain runs the {wiki:Dream Sand River}: use the water with the {item:Delicate Pan}. Possible results:
- *"You sieve the water, but without luck."* — nothing;
- *"You found some useless pebbles and crystals."* — {item:Remains of a Crude Dream};
- *"You find some dream sand nuggets in your pan."* — {item:Dream Sand};
- *"You accidentally drop the pan in the whirling water."* — you lose the pan.
Keep using the water until you lose the pan (recommended), to collect as much Dream Sand as possible.

Within those 10 seconds, use the {item:Dream Nebuliser} on the {item:Traces of an Ancient Dream}. Results:
- *"You blasted the dream to pieces."* — failed, you receive {item:Remains of a Crude Dream};
- *"The nebuliser accidentally liberated hostile living energy."* — failed, a {creature:Feversleep} or {creature:Terrorsleep} spawns;
- *"You successfully removed an Ancient Dream from the rock."* — you receive an {item:Ancient Dream}.
The lanterns recover in 2.5 minutes and the rocks in 5 minutes; you can use several.
